WEBVTT

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:09.460
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the twelfth. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the Teams mime again?</v>

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.759
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, you're coming through. Bit tinny, but we're used to that.</v>

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:25.760
<v Callum Reid>I'm in the portakabin. The heating in here seems to have two settings: absolutely nothing and blast furnace. Just moaning, before that goes on a list.</v>

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:30.559
<v Grace Liu>Good clarification. I could practically hear the action log opening.</v>

00:00:31.859 --> 00:00:36.759
<v Tomasz Nowak>There's a birthday cake in the office, anyway. That has improved the Monday situation.</v>

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.619
<v Jamie Brennan>Whose birthday?</v>

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:45.789
<v Tomasz Nowak>No idea. Didn't want to hold up the cake asking technical questions.</v>

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:54.950
<v Hannah Price>And there's the charity bake sale on Friday. Not volunteering us for anything, just saying it's a dangerous week for cake.</v>

00:00:57.229 --> 00:00:58.979
<v Callum Reid>Excellent. A balanced diet, then.</v>

00:01:01.009 --> 00:01:05.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we spend the whole stand-up on sponge. What's already closed out?</v>

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.799
<v Hannah Price>I signed off the inspection on the cooling tower on Tuesday. That's finished, nothing outstanding from that inspection.</v>

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:18.459
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Hannah. Closed, not another one for today.</v>

00:01:19.299 --> 00:01:26.650
<v Callum Reid>And I tested the GT2 yesterday and it's all fine now. That's the completed test, not a request for another run.</v>

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.810
<v Jamie Brennan>On GT2—sorry, slightly different thing—the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the GT2 bearing.</v>

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:40.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, separate issue. That delivery's still blocked on their confirmation; we're not adding a fresh chasing action here.</v>

00:01:42.609 --> 00:01:46.810
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly. Just don't want 'test fine' to sound like the bearing's arrived.</v>

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:53.250
<v Tomasz Nowak>I already swapped the filter on the waste heat boiler yesterday as well. That one's done.</v>

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:57.379
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, saw that in the handover. No repeat job there.</v>

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you order spare parts for the HV board? That's fairly important.</v>

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:09.729
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll order spare parts for the HV board. Understood, fairly important.</v>

00:02:12.009 --> 00:02:15.860
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, you clipped a bit there. Was that the HV board?</v>

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:21.419
<v Jamie Brennan>The HV board, yeah. That's the order I'm taking.</v>

00:02:22.639 --> 00:02:27.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Jamie. No separate deadline on that one, just the priority we've said.</v>

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:32.210
<v Grace Liu>Got it. Audio's doing that little underwater thing for me too.</v>

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:37.409
<v Callum Reid>It's Monday. Even the Wi-Fi hasn't warmed up.</v>

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:46.250
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, the other one: can you swap the filter on the CT1 after lunch, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:02:46.979 --> 00:02:52.930
<v Jamie Brennan>I can't take that one, sorry. I haven't got the hands-on cover to leave stores after lunch.</v>

00:02:55.419 --> 00:03:03.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, not with Jamie then. Olumide, could you swap the filter on the CT1 after lunch, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:12.620
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll take that instead. I'll swap the filter on the CT1 after lunch, if I've got a spare minute.</v>

00:03:13.409 --> 00:03:17.960
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's the CT1 one, not the waste heat boiler one I just mentioned.</v>

00:03:19.039 --> 00:03:21.840
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, CT1. Yours is already done; different filter.</v>

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:27.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Olumide has that now, not Jamie, and it's a spare-minute job after lunch.</v>

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:34.370
<v Jamie Brennan>Thanks. Didn't want to say yes and then leave everyone thinking it was covered by me.</v>

00:03:34.729 --> 00:03:39.280
<v Callum Reid>Makes a change from the usual enthusiastic yes followed by a disappearing act.</v>

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:48.030
<v Olumide Adeyemi>While I've got the mic, I'll sort the training records for the new starters next week. No rush on that.</v>

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.759
<v Grace Liu>The records, rather than another training session, yeah?</v>

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:57.620
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, just sorting the training records for the new starters. That's what I'm volunteering for.</v>

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Olumide. Next week, no rush. Agreed.</v>

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:04.990
<v Grace Liu>Fine. Just keeping the wording straight, not adding anything else.</v>

00:04:07.319 --> 00:04:11.870
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, fair. 'Training' on its own ends up meaning about six different things.</v>

00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:19.819
<v Hannah Price>I'll inspect the boiler safety valve for leaks on Friday. I'll drop everything for that one.</v>

00:04:22.319 --> 00:04:25.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Hannah. So on Friday, that's the one taking precedence.</v>

00:04:26.639 --> 00:04:33.639
<v Hannah Price>Exactly. On Friday, not pulling it forward to this morning, but drop everything for that one when it comes round.</v>

00:04:34.439 --> 00:04:38.290
<v Grace Liu>Understood. The high priority and the Friday timing are both clear.</v>

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:44.699
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, I spoke over the end there—wasn't disputing it. Your audio just caught up with mine.</v>

00:04:46.439 --> 00:04:50.639
<v Hannah Price>No worries. Teams makes us all sound like we're having an argument.</v>

00:04:51.649 --> 00:04:53.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's agreed, Hannah.</v>

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:58.649
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll replace the seals on the Water Booster Pump next Tuesday.</v>

00:05:01.139 --> 00:05:04.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Next Tuesday for the Water Booster Pump seals, Tomasz. That's agreed.</v>

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:09.399
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, next Tuesday. That's the seal replacement I'm taking.</v>

00:05:10.959 --> 00:05:12.160
<v Callum Reid>Mm, clear.</v>

00:05:13.459 --> 00:05:15.560
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, heard that properly this time.</v>

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:21.790
<v Tomasz Nowak>And I'll book a contractor to look at the water system today. No rush, though.</v>

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:26.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Booking today, rather than saying the contractor has to be here today?</v>

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:35.269
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's it. I'll make the booking today. No rush within today, and I'm not giving a visit date.</v>

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:41.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed, Tomasz. Book a contractor to look at the water system today, no rush.</v>

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:46.699
<v Grace Liu>Good distinction. Booking and attendance aren't the same deadline.</v>

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:51.490
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah. Otherwise someone hears 'today' and expects a van at the gate.</v>

00:05:52.899 --> 00:05:58.149
<v Sarah Okafor>Any observations before we finish? Not extra jobs disguised as an 'oh, by the way'.</v>

00:06:00.629 --> 00:06:09.379
<v Tomasz Nowak>Just an observation: I saw the pressure on the pick and place on two dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:12.899
<v Callum Reid>Right, a brief dip and recovered by itself.</v>

00:06:13.529 --> 00:06:17.730
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah. Just reporting what I saw, not raising a job for today.</v>

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:24.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. We've separated the completed bits and the supplier blocker from the agreed work. Everyone clear?</v>

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:26.490
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, all clear.</v>

00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:32.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Thanks, everyone. I'll let you escape the little squares.</v>
